<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Where a cubic is increasing or decreasing</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The function \(f(x) = {@f@}\) is [[if test="is(a0>0)"]]decreasing[[else]]increasing[[/if]] for \(a \lt x \lt b\), and nowhere else.</p><p>(a) Find \(a\) and \(b\).</p><div>\(a =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] \(\quad b =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) For which values of \(x\) is \(f\) [[if test="is(a0>0)"]]increasing[[else]]decreasing[[/if]]?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A function is increasing where its gradient is positive and decreasing where its gradient is negative.</p><p>\[f'(x) = {@df@} = {@dfac@}\]so \(f'(x) = 0\) at \(x = {@p0@}\) and \(x = {@q0@}\).</p><p>[[if test="is(a0>0)"]]The coefficient of \(x^2\) in \(f'(x)\) is positive, so \(f'(x)\) is negative between its roots and positive outside them.[[else]]The coefficient of \(x^2\) in \(f'(x)\) is negative, so \(f'(x)\) is positive between its roots and negative outside them.[[/if]]</p><p>(a) \(f\) is [[if test="is(a0>0)"]]decreasing[[else]]increasing[[/if]] for \({@p0@} \lt x \lt {@q0@}\): \(a = {@p0@}\), \(b = {@q0@}\).</p><p>(b) \(f\) is [[if test="is(a0>0)"]]increasing[[else]]decreasing[[/if]] for \(x \lt {@p0@}\) and for \(x \gt {@q0@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: interval of increase or decrease. a0 > 0: f decreasing between the roots of f'; a0 < 0: increasing. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 9, section B, Example 3 and Exercise B question 1. */
L: [[1,-1,3,2],[2,-2,1,5],[-1,-3,1,4],[1,1,5,-2],[-2,-1,2,3],[2,-3,-1,1],[-1,2,4,-6],[-1,-4,2,7],[-2,-4,-1,2],[2,2,5,-3]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
a0: L[ix][1]; p0: L[ix][2]; q0: L[ix][3]; d0: L[ix][4];
f: expand((a0)*x^3-3*(a0)*((p0)+(q0))/2*x^2+3*(a0)*(p0)*(q0)*x+(d0));
df: diff(f,x);
dfac: 3*a0*(x-p0)*(x-q0);
opts: [["in",false,"between a and b only"],["out",true,"for x less than a, and for x greater than b"],["right",false,"for x greater than b only"]];]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
