  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Differentiation II: where a function is increasing or decreasing</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.1: Find the interval where a cubic is decreasing (or increasing) from the roots of its derivative, and where it does the opposite.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Example 3 in Section B and Question 1 in Exercise B of Chapter 9 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: randomised over curated cubics, with the sign of the leading coefficient deciding which interval is asked for.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
